hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1454","The Prophet (ﷺ) said, ""The most true words said by a poet was the words of Labid."" He said, Verily, Everything except Allah is perishable and Umaiya bin As-Salt was about to be a Muslim (but he did not embrace Islam)."
"1455","Allah's Messenger (ﷺ) said, ""If Allah makes us victorious, our encamping place will be Al-Khaif, the place where the infidels took an oath to be loyal to Heathenism (by boycotting Banu Hashim, the Prophet's folk)."
